      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "A vintage Rider-Waite tarot card illustration, bold pen-and-ink woodcut linework with flat muted earthy color, aged paper texture. A single hooded robed figure stands at the center beneath a great unfinished stone arch, holding aloft one glowing golden wedge-shaped keystone, reaching to set it into the open apex of the arch. Twin stone pillars frame the figure. Scattered dressed stones and a mason's mallet, chisel and hanging plumb line rest at the figure's feet. Through the arch a path leads to a luminous violet dawn horizon with a temple span beyond. Symmetrical composition, warm golden glow against cool grey-blue stone, hushed reverent atmosphere, hand-drawn storybook illustration, no text."
      ]
